{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q020_syntaxin_fragment_reclassification","answer":"Verified SCOPe facts (release 2.08, current stable, freeze 2021-07-28). All three structures are classified in the same lineage: class a (All alpha), fold a.47 STAT-like (sunid 47654; fold comment '4 long helices; bundle, left-handed twist (coiled coil); right-handed superhelix'), superfamily a.47.2 t-snare proteins (47661), family a.47.2.1 t-snare proteins (47662). 1br0 chain A = d1br0a_ (sunid 17772) and 1ez3 chains A/B/C = d1ez3a_/d1ez3b_/d1ez3c_ (17768-17770) sit under the curated protein node 'Syntaxin 1A N-terminal domain' (47663), rat species (47664). Each of these four fragment domains carries the curator comment 'three-helical fragment; similar to one spectrin repeat' and the per-domain heterogeneity/inconsistency flag 'ms' = 'missing some secondary structures that made up less than one-third of the common domain'. Observed ATOM lengths: d1br0a_ 120 residues, d1ez3a_ 124. 1dn1 was obsoleted on 2008-03-25 by 3c98. In 2.08, 1dn1 chain B = d1dn1b_ (new sunid 302344) is placed under the protein node 'automated matches' (191190) with the comment 'automated match to d3c98b_' and no heterogeneity flags; observed length 222. The curated full-domain reference is now d3c98b_ (173092), 230 observed residues, under protein node 47663, with no flags. Historical change verified by querying release 1.75 separately: there d1dn1b_ had sunid 17771 under the curated protein node 47663 with no caveats; in 2.08 it was re-entered as an automated match to the superseding entry. The API documents the obsolescence and the re-entry; no further curatorial rationale is stated. The fold node carries the warning 'SCOPe levels above superfamily do not imply homology'. Quality (representative selection only, not homology): 1ez3 X-ray 1.9 A, SPACI 0.468; 3c98 X-ray 2.6 A, SPACI 0.312; 1dn1 X-ray 2.6 A, SPACI 0.255; 1br0 NMR, SPACI 0.036.

Interpretation. (1) The fragments were never mis-folded, but SCOPe's current treatment makes explicit that their fold assignment is inherited by homology from the complete syntaxin 1A N-terminal domain (the 'common domain' the ms flag refers to), which is represented by the full-length chain B of 3c98/1dn1. A three-helix fragment does not by itself satisfy the four-long-helix definition of fold a.47; the assignment is a family-level homology placement, not independent evidence that the fragment adopts the STAT-like fold. (2) The curator comment that the fragment resembles one spectrin repeat is a warning that a three-helix fragment judged alone could be matched to an unrelated fold. That is fold-level structural similarity only; SCOPe asserts no homology between syntaxin and spectrin repeats, and the resemblance must not be strengthened into either a homology or an 'analogy/convergence' claim. (3) The full-chain domain in 3c98 B / 1dn1 B, as classified, spans more of the protein than the fragments (222-230 vs 120-124 observed residues) and SCOPe treats the whole chain as one domain; fragment coordinates from 1br0 or 1ez3 cannot serve as templates for regions they do not contain, and any statements about the closed conformation, the linker/H3 region or Munc18 (nSec1) binding come from the literature, not from SCOPe placement. (4) Because 1dn1 is obsolete and now only an automated match, d3c98b_ should be cited as the curated full-domain reference, with 1dn1 only as its superseded predecessor; 1ez3 remains the best-quality coordinates for the three-helix region but is still a flagged fragment. (5) Function transfer is limited to what the family level implies: shared family a.47.2.1 (which also contains e.g. the yeast Sso1 protein node) supports common ancestry among t-SNARE N-terminal domains, not identical SNARE-complex behavior; fold a.47 membership shared with other superfamilies implies no common ancestry.

Limits. SCOPe records state that the fragments lack secondary structure elements but not which helices or how they align to the full domain; that requires an inspected alignment. The 1.75-to-2.08 change for d1dn1b_ is documented only as obsolescence plus an automated match. No BLAST/FATCAT hit streams were retrieved, so no non-official relationships are proposed.","evidence_used":["scop-homology/SKILL.md","mcp__scope__get_scop_service_info","mcp__scope__get_scop_pdb_entry","mcp__scope__get_scop_domains","mcp__scope__get_scop_node","mcp__scope__list_scop_children","mcp__scope__get_scop_sequence","mcp__scope__compare_structure_quality","/api/v1/releases/current","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1br0","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1br0/chains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1br0/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1br0/quality","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1ez3","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1ez3/chains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1ez3/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1ez3/quality","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1dn1","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1dn1/chains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1dn1/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/1dn1/quality","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/3c98","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/3c98/domains","/api/v1/releases/2.08/pdb/3c98/quality","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1br0a_","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1br0a_/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1br0a_/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1br0a_/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1ez3a_","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1ez3a_/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1ez3a_/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1ez3a_/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1ez3b_/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1ez3b_/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1ez3c_/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1ez3c_/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1dn1b_","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1dn1b_/parents","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1dn1b_/annotations","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1dn1b_/homology","/api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d3